"""W3C family data (wave 3 phase 2): the 21 prepared test-capture and readiness families.

Literal data only, shared by the checker (scripts/pm_w3c_event_oracles.py) and the fixture builder
(scripts/pm-w3c-cases.py). It holds names, owner units, payload-to-source joins and, per family clause,
the source fact it reads and where a one-defect witness changes it. It decides no verdict: each clause's
predicate is written in the checker (``CLAUSE_FACTS``) and emitted into its guard-table row.

Owner text: TCME-1300..TCME-1319 and ATS-1220 (family predicates, numbered transition clauses), CV-1300..CV-1320
(payloads), SP-1300..SP-1320 (Storage). Each clause tuple is
``(row suffix, refusal code, words, template, literal or None, witness edit)``; a witness edit is
``(stage, pointer, value)``, applied by the builder before the stages that derive copies from it.
"""

